  "reason": "The current best is config_037 (scvi_n200 + ViT-L, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at 0.7062 acc. The two remaining untested design axes for this strongest encoder pair are aggregation (transformer) and fusion (concat). Aggregation has shown the larger historical effect (avgpool beat transformer by ~4-6 pp with PCA+ResNet50), so testing whether that ordering holds with the best encoders is the higher-value question. Config_039 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) isolates the aggregation variable while keeping the best fusion (weighted) fixed. If transformer underperforms avgpool again, it confirms avgpool is robustly superior across encoder quality levels and we can lock that choice; if it matches or exceeds config_037, it reveals that stronger encoders change the aggregation dynamics. This is the most informative single experiment for reducing uncertainty about the aggregation design decision in the region of the search space where performance is highest."
}

